sdbus-c++ v2.3.1 for Slackware -current (x86_64)
================================================

What it is
----------
sdbus-c++ is a high-level C++ library for D-Bus built on top of sd-bus
(systemd's D-Bus stack). It lets C++ code expose and call D-Bus services
generated from XML service definitions. Noctalia uses it for system D-Bus
communication.

Upstream: https://github.com/Kistler-Group/sdbus-cpp
License: LGPL-2.1-only (with linking exception); see COPYING / COPYING-LGPL-Exception

Dependencies
------------
* Build: gcc/g++ (C++17), CMake, pkg-config, ninja
* Runtime link: libelogind (elogind is installed on this system).
  The library also accepts libsystemd or basu, but only elogind's pkg-config
  module ("libelogind", >= 238) is present here, so the build uses it. No
  libsystemd or FetchContent/network access is required.

Install layout
--------------
  /usr/lib64/libsdbus-c++.so.2.3.1 (+ SONAME/dev symlinks)
  /usr/include/sdbus-c++/          (public headers)
  /usr/lib64/pkgconfig/sdbus-c++.pc
  /usr/lib64/cmake/sdbus-c++/      (CMake package config)

Build options used (all in the .SlackBuild)
-------------------------------------------
  -DSDBUSCPP_BUILD_TESTS=OFF
  -DSDBUSCPP_BUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF
  -DSDBUSCPP_BUILD_DOCS=OFF
  -DSDBUSCPP_BUILD_CODEGEN=OFF
  -DBUILD_SHARED_LIBS=ON

Source + checksum
-----------------
No tarball is published on the release page, so the GitHub archive is used:

  https://github.com/Kistler-Group/sdbus-cpp/archive/refs/tags/v2.3.1.tar.gz
  MD5SUM  518781362360e93ab5658d86baab1c47
  SHA256  3a289eded586c26d06c1387de72c7bf7c809527a70d51ba6401fe61059b19626

The archive extracts to a top-level `sdbus-cpp-2.3.1/` directory.
Download into the build dir and name it sdbus-cpp-2.3.1.tar.gz:

  cd libraries/sdbus-cpp
  source ./sdbus-cpp.info
  wget -c $DOWNLOAD
  mv v2.3.1.tar.gz sdbus-cpp-2.3.1.tar.gz
  ./sdbus-cpp.SlackBuild
